\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Community Development Director Masa Alkire provided a brief statement and introduced Traffic Engineer Erik Zandvliet who provided the PowerPoint presentation.\line\line Walker Consultants Principal/Director of Studies Steffen Turoff provided a brief statement and introduced Consultant Jeff Weckstein who continued with the PowerPoint presentation.\line\line Consultant Weckstein and Traffic Engineer Zandvliet responded to City Council questions.\line\line Walker Consultants Principal/Director of Studies Turoff continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Strategy 1: Parking Rate Structures and Time Limits.\line\line Traffic Engineer Zandvliet responded to City Council questions.\line\line Walker Consultants Principal/Director of Studies Turoff continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Strategy 4: District Wide Valet & Attended Parking.\line\line Walker Consultants Principal/Director of Studies Turoff and Traffic Engineer Zandvliet responded to City Council questions.\line\line\cf1 Mayor Lesser opened the floor to public comments. The following individual(s) spoke:\line\line Jim Burton\line Kelly Stroman\line JonathanTolkin\line\line Seeing no further requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comments.\line\line Traffic Engineer Zandvliet, \cf0 Consultant Weckstein and Walker Consultants Principal/Director of Studies Turoff \cf1 responded to City Council questions.\line\line\b See attached document for voting details on the Short-Term Parking Strategy Summary.\line\line\cf0\b0 Consultant Weckstein continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Strategy 6: Technology & Wayfinding.\line\line Traffic Engineer Zandvliet, Walker Consultants Principal/Director of Studies Turoff and Consultant Weckstein responded to City Council questions. \line\line\cf1 Mayor Lesser opened the floor to public comments. The following individual(s) spoke:\line\line Kelly Stroman\line Jim Burton\line Jill Lamkin\line\line Seeing no further requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comments.\line\line Traffic Engineer Zandvliet and Finance Director Libby Bretthauer responded to City Council questions.\line\line\b See attached document for voting details \cf0 on the Long Term Parking Strategy Summary.\cf1\b0\i0\f1\line\line\cf0\i\f0 At 7:02 PM, the City Council recessed and reconvened at 7:16 PM with all City Councilmembers present.\line\line Consultant Turoff continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Strategy 9: Enforcement Hours.\line\line Traffic Engineer Zandvliet, Senior Planner Jaehee Yoon, Police Chief Rachel Johnson, and City Manager Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line\cf1 Mayor Lesser opened the floor to public comments. The following individual(s) spoke:\line\line Kelly Stroman\line\line Seeing no further requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comments.\line\line\cf0 Traffic Engineer Zandvliet responded to City Council questions.\line\line\b See attached document for voting details on the Enforcement, Dynamic Pricing, and Loading Strategy Summary.\line\line\b0 Consultant Turoff continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Strategy 13: Parking Requirements.\line\line Consultant Turoff, Traffic Engineer Zandvliet and City Manager Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line\cf1 Mayor Lesser opened the floor to public comments.\line\line Seeing no requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comments.\line\line Traffic Engineer Zandvliet, City Manager Mirzakhanian and Planning Manager Adam Finestone responded to City Council questions.\line\line\cf0\b See attached document for voting details on the Future Parking Supply & Funding Options Strategy Summary.\line\line\b0 Consultant Turoff continued with the PowerPoint presentation on \cf1 Strategy 17: Bicycle Parking.\cf0\line\line Traffic Engineer Zandvliet and City Manager Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line At 8:28 PM, City Council recessed and reconvened at 8:33 PM with all City Councilmembers present.\line\line\cf1 Mayor Lesser opened the floor to public comments. The following individual(s) spoke:\line\line Jill Lamkin\line\line Seeing no further requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comments.\line\line Traffic Engineer Zandvliet and City Manager Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line\cf0\b See attached document for voting details on the Bicycle Parking, Micromobility, and TDM Strategy Summary.\line\line\cf1 The City Council directed staff to return at a future meeting with a summary list of all items approved during this meeting, and to return early next year to allow City Council to determine priority items.\i0\line\line\b0\i City Manager Mirzakhanian and Traffic Engineer Zandvliet responded to City Council questions.\i0\f1\par
